📖 INTRODUCTION TO THE LIKE OPERATOR
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The LIKE operator is used in a WHERE clause to search for a specified PATTERN within
a column's text data. This is one of the most powerful operators in SQL for flexible
string matching and pattern searching.

KEY FEATURES:
• Used with WHERE clause for pattern-based filtering
• Case-insensitive by default in MySQL
• Works with wildcard characters (% and _)
• Can be combined with AND/OR operators
• Essential for search functionality in applications

COMMON USE CASES:
• Search bars in web applications
• Filter data by partial matches
• Email and username searches
• Address lookups
• Product descriptions
• Data validation


