📚 COMPARISON: LIKE vs OTHER OPERATORS
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

┌──────────┬──────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Operator │ Purpose                          │ Example                            │
├──────────┼──────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ =        │ Exact match                      │ WHERE City = 'Berlin'              │
│ LIKE     │ Pattern matching with wildcards  │ WHERE City LIKE 'ber%'             │
│ IN       │ Match any value in list          │ WHERE City IN ('Berlin','London')  │
│ BETWEEN  │ Match within range               │ WHERE Age BETWEEN 18 AND 65        │
│ >        │ Greater than                     │ WHERE Age > 18                     │
│ <        │ Less than                        │ WHERE Age < 65                     │
│ >=       │ Greater than or equal            │ WHERE Age >= 18                    │
│ <=       │ Less than or equal               │ WHERE Age <= 65                    │
│ <>       │ Not equal                        │ WHERE City <> 'Berlin'             │
│ NOT LIKE │ Inverse pattern matching         │ WHERE City NOT LIKE 'ber%'         │
│ REGEXP   │ Regular expression matching      │ WHERE Email REGEXP '^[^@]+@'       │
│ ISNULL   │ Check for NULL                   │ WHERE City IS NULL                 │
└──────────┴──────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘


