🎓 SUMMARY & KEY TAKEAWAYS
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. SYNTAX:
   SELECT * FROM table WHERE column LIKE pattern;

2. WILDCARDS:
   • % = Zero or more characters
   • _ = Exactly one character

3. COMMON PATTERNS:
   • 'text%' → Starts with (efficient)
   • '%text' → Ends with (less efficient)
   • '%text%' → Contains (least efficient)

4. KEY FEATURES:
   • Case-insensitive by default
   • Can use NOT LIKE for inverse matching
   • Can combine with AND/OR operators
   • NULL values never match patterns

5. PERFORMANCE:
   • Leading % prevents index usage
   • Combine with other conditions to narrow results
   • Use FULLTEXT for large text searches

6. BEST PRACTICES:
   • Always use LIKE (not =) for patterns
   • Put most restrictive conditions first
   • Consider using indexes for better performance
   • Handle NULL values explicitly if needed
   • Use BINARY for case-sensitive matching

